- **Minute-by-minute scheduler**: Dynamic reallocation of resources and memory pool management
- **Preemption and throttling rules**: Handling SLA pressure from high-CKNE tenants
- **Additional considerations**: Telemetry, fairness guarantees, and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// CKNE-to-batch sizing mapping
function getBatchSizeForCKNE(ckne) {
  if (ckne >= 0.8) return 32;  // Premium tier
  if (ckne >= 0.5) return 16;  // Standard tier
  if (ckne >= 0.2) return 8;   // Budget tier
  return 4;                    // Minimal SLA
}

// Minute-by-minute scheduler
setInterval(() => {
  const activeTenants = getActiveTenants();
  const gpuMemory = getAvailableMemory();
  const slaBreaches = checkSLABreaches();

  // Preempt low-CKNE tenants under SLA pressure
  slaBreaches.forEach(tenant => {
    if (tenant.ckne < 0.5) {
      throttleTenant(tenant.id, 0.5);
    }
  });

  // Reallocate memory pools based on CKNE distribution
  reallocateMemoryPools(activeTenants);
}, 60000);
```

